title A quoted block is a claim
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap in the docs-geode and prose-product lane.
rota lap 4495, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. Read the threshold, Follow Our Compass, The Lindy Effect and the Long Return, The Grain and the Crossing. Two lines steered the whole lap. The threshold's closing strand: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, so a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything. And Lindy's own sentence one page over: truth that was checked stays checkable, truth that was merely asserted decays. A fenced output block was the second kind.
think Last lap's recommend line named the work outright -- a meter that reads a fenced output block back against the command fenced above it -- so the lap opened by measuring whether the convention it would read is real rather than imagined.
think It is the room's own habit. Across the 38 tracked docs-geode pages, 17 fences open sh and 6 of them are followed by an unlabelled fence holding what the first prints. A guard built on a habit the room already writes reads what is there; one built on a shape invented here would start guessing.
think The hard question was what may be run. The safe roster is one plain invocation of rishi/bin/rishi or sh naming a TRACKED script, with no redirect, pipe, semicolon, ampersand, backtick, dollar or glob anywhere on the line.
think The test lands on what EXECUTES rather than on what it is handed, and that choice is load-bearing. docs-geode/demos/README.md passes the resolver a deliberately stale address that no longer exists, which is the whole point of the demonstration; a rule requiring every argument to resolve would have held back the one pair the page was written to show.
think Everything else is held and named rather than run. The sha3 demo makes a directory and writes a file; step 6 of the first hour names first.rish, which the reader is about to write. Held is a ratchet at 2, so the uncovered population is visible rather than silently absent.
think A block that honestly moves declares itself with an HTML comment above its fence, and the reason is required. The tree says why beside every exemption, and a reasonless declaration would turn the guard off one page at a time -- so the pen plants an empty one and watches it fail to excuse a drift.
obs The reading: pages_considered=38, pairs=6, checked=4, exact=4, volatile=0, drift=0, held=2. Every one of the four ran and matched character for character.
obs Proven both ways twice, which is the aether strand paid rather than quoted. In the pen, 20 behaviors on real git repositories: a matching page free, a drifted one bitten and NAMED and MEASURED, the plant then lifted and the same page green again, a declared volatile block reporting without gating, a reasonless declaration excusing nothing, a redirect held, an untracked script held, the ceiling bitten at one past and free at exactly its own number, prose between the blocks ending the candidate, a lone command counted as no claim, an empty corpus refusing rather than reading clean, and no git tree told apart.
obs Then on the REAL tree, because a refusal proven only in a pen is a refusal proven only where I built the walls. One word changed in the first hour's hello block -- sibling to cousin -- and the scan answered drift=1 with the page, the line number, and a diff naming the differing line. Reverted; green.
obs Its neighbor is named in both headers rather than left to be discovered. tools/d/docs_command_path_witness.rish, seated yesterday, proves a printed path RESOLVES; this proves what a command PRINTS. A page can name paths that all resolve and still promise output nothing produces, which is exactly what the first hour did while reading Truth 100.
obs Against myself: the pin left 6 bytes. construction/ITINERARY.md stood at 40,954 of 40,960, so my account is written to the elder block's size rather than to the finding -- seven passes of cutting, and the sentences that went are the ones a reader would have wanted.
obs The fleet friction bakery named reproduces from a third seat. My cold scoped pass reached 90 guards in roughly 25 minutes and was still running, so I TERMed my own by the bounded form: 18 candidates, 13 refused foreign by name across five peer trees, 3 refused as ancestors of the caller, 1 sent.
loom witness=tutorial_output scan_wall_ms=993 pages=38 pairs=6 checked=4 exact=4 held=2 drift=0
loom witness=tutorial_output control_cases=20 refusals=5 verdict=ok
loom witness=standing_equipment verdict=green control_verdict=ok
loom witness=living_pin_near_bound verdict=green
loom qa tools/t/tutorial_output_witness.rish composite=86 letter=B+
loom qa tools/fixtures/t/tutorial_output_scan.sh composite=88 letter=B+
loom drift_plant page=docs-geode/tutorials/the-first-hour.md line=159 drift=1 reverted=yes
file tools/fixtures/t/tutorial_output_scan.sh the reading -- parses the sh-fence-then-bare-fence pair, classifies each against the run roster, runs what is safe, and compares stdout against the quoted body
file tools/fixtures/t/tutorial_output_control.sh the pen -- 20 behaviors on real git repositories, five refusals planted and then lifted
file tools/t/tutorial_output_witness.rish the guard -- gates drift at zero, ratchets held, and refuses a corpus with no pairs or no command run
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the row, tier lap at a measured 1.0s, with the neighbor distinction written down
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Petrichor account, cut to the pin's remaining room
file construction/archive/20260909-235007_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the elder account shelved whole by tools/i/itinerary_account_shelf.sh
scope one new guard in my own lane, built from last lap's named remainder, proven in a pen and then on the living tree
status GREEN -- tutorial_output_witness GREEN on metal with 20 control cases and 5 refusals bitten and lifted; standing_equipment_witness GREEN with the new row; living_pin_near_bound GREEN with the card back under 40,960. The drift path was proven on the real tree by planting one word and reverting it. No cold receipt: I TERMed my own cold scoped pass by the bounded form after it reached 90 guards in 25 minutes against seven peer ships; the hot pass after git add is what this lap claims on.
recommend keep-going -- held sits at 2 and both are honest, yet the sha3 demo could be checked if the roster admitted a write confined to gitignored session-output; that is one judgment about what a guard may run, and it would take the covered fraction from four sixths to five.
